{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790291812,"nonce":"1XGPkuM500NxeZkhJtFlLAApSBI=","title":"eq(\"literal\", \u003cDynamic expression\u003e) crashes: generic call specializes on String while the argument is a Dynamic","message":"Issue10041, Issue11007, Issue9217 and Issue8975 crash in `eq(\"hi\", \u003creflection read or switch result typed Dynamic\u003e)`. The generic `eq\u003cT\u003e` specializes with T = String from the literal, and the Dynamic argument reaches the String slot unconverted.\n\nCasting every Dynamic argument to the String a sibling binds fixes all four. It LOST Issue10834, though: `a.toString()` on `a:Dynamic = []` returns void rather than \"[]\", and the cast carried that into a String comparison that crashes. Two parts: make Dynamic method calls on arrays return their value, then widen the conversion (calls.rs unify_dynamic_arguments, currently unannotated parameters only).\n\nAlso: `Str(s, null)` against an omitted optional enum argument matches the enum's first constructor, because a nullary constructor and null share a representation.","files":null}]}